Package: rufus-linux
Version: 0.6.0
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Rufus Linux Port Contributors <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-4.0 (>= 4.10), udisks2, util-linux, dosfstools
Recommends: xorriso, wimtools, exfatprogs, ntfs-3g, e2fsprogs, fdisk, mtools, 7zip, grub-common, pkexec
Suggests: grub-pc-bin, grub-efi-amd64-bin, grub-efi-arm64-bin, grub-efi-arm-bin
Description: Native Linux preview of the Rufus bootable USB utility
 GTK 4 frontend and CLI for verified image writing, removable-drive formatting,
 BIOS/UEFI Windows installation media, persistent Linux live media, and FreeDOS.
 This is an experimental Linux port with a separate backend; it does not provide
 full Windows feature parity.
